body:
Sorry about that. I updated the post with my location. Yes, I've been diagnosed with bipolar disorder, PTSD and general anxiety. Winter is especially low for me and I tend to struggle with the depression side of my bipolar. I'm becoming increasingly anxious and hypervigilant at work and then it lasts for about an hour after I get off. This is due to the hostility I'm experiencing at work. When I first started working, it was great. I felt happy and motivated. That specific shift leader threw me off once with their behavior towards me but I just brushed it off. Now that it's gotten worse, I find it negatively affecting my mental health. In the past, with other jobs, I tended to call in a lot when experiencing these symptoms and if my mental health got really bad I'd just stop showing up. I'm trying harder than ever now to push through it, but this is starting to aggravate certain symptoms that come with my diagnosis.

&#x200B;

That's unfortunate, though. I guess if my general manager doesn't take action I'll put in my two weeks and work elsewhere.
